{"id": "EUVD-2026-82038", "enisaUuid": "8ae90361-5d13-323a-8df1-31f9292d0c84", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: fix RX data queuing of RRO 3.0\n\nFor RRO 3.0, RX data released from a RRO data queue should be put to\nthe indicator queue. The frames are processed and completed in the\ncontext of the indicator queue NAPI, which only polls skbs queued on\nthe MT_RXQ_RRO_IND list; frames queued under the data queue id are\nleft sitting on that list until the data queue NAPI happens to run,\nstalling and reordering RX data.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62aea1d45b524cde9e02d1e7f65d2c4fd60871b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db4be207f3f6d8886f0b31f8c7db863a4b835ec1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86897f106669c07eea4c34b54c3268d448d41426"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90377", "GHSA-57wf-22jg-j93r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4f1b6c87-c8cb-3ba3-9bad-08416c75fcc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "524192cf-f1c7-32c6-a34c-383950bb958d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7819329e-05e0-3066-90a6-a3f5b2938d05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "86552e19-3c87-38ff-bdb5-533f0b25f7e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1e58e137b61693f12da037d2d50aca9c2140a43 <62aea1d45b524cde9e02d1e7f65d2c4fd60871b8"}, {"id": "86f27a9d-738a-34b4-a709-8a3d0fa1e95d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "9ee5daaa-ec13-318a-93e8-4d5dfd9b3750", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1e58e137b61693f12da037d2d50aca9c2140a43 <86897f106669c07e